SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/home/{{STOCKEY_USER}}/.local/bin
MAILTO=""

STOCKEY_DIR={{STOCKEY_DIR}}
LOG_DIR={{LOG_DIR}}

# Create log directory once before enabling the crontab:
#   mkdir -p {{LOG_DIR}}
#
# Run with go-crond:
#   ./go-crond {{GENERATED_CRONTAB}} --allow-unprivileged
#
# This file includes a username field. Remove that field before installing into a normal per-user crontab.
#
# Pure-TA cut (2026-08-02, PURE_TA_MIGRATION_PLAN.md Phase 4): only the 6 data-platform
# jobs below remain. All advisory/paper-trading/research/frontend jobs were removed here;
# their code lives on the advisory-archive-2026-07 branch until Phase 4 fully archives it.
#
# Fundamentals screener (2026-08-11, docs/FUNDAMENTAL_SCREENER_PRD.md): a deliberate,
# separate carve-out from the pure-TA boundary above -- long-term fundamental screening
# (screener/watchlist/narrative/portfolio), not technicals/trading. Two more jobs below:
# the batch pipeline (fundamentals/run_pipeline.py) and its API server
# (fundamentals/api/app.py), which serves the screener/ Nuxt frontend.
#
# TIMEZONE (2026-08-13, confirmed empirically via logs/cron/*.log real firing
# timestamps): this go-crond build (webdevops/go-crond 23.12.0) does NOT honor a
# CRON_TZ line -- there used to be one here and jobs fired at its literal UTC
# numbers instead of IST-shifted ones. The server's system clock is UTC
# (timedatectl: Etc/UTC) with no sudo to change it, and go-crond has no
# --timezone flag and no documented CRON_TZ/TZ support. Every schedule below is
# therefore written in UTC directly, with the intended IST wall-clock time noted
# in each comment -- IST = UTC + 5:30, so UTC = IST - 5:30. All of today's IST
# times are >= 06:50 IST, comfortably clear of the 05:30 IST / 00:00 UTC
# boundary, so none of these conversions cross a UTC calendar day and the
# weekday ("1-5") fields are unaffected. If a future job is intended for early
# IST morning (before ~05:30 IST), remember it lands on the PREVIOUS UTC date
# and its weekday field needs shifting too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recurring cron-managed jobs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SCHEDULE DESIGN (retimed 2026-09-02) -- crawl each source just AFTER it publishes,
# and keep a guaranteed morning catch-up behind it.
#
# The old schedule was set by convenience, not by when data actually appears, and every
# downstream failure this repo has chased traced back to that. Measured evidence:
#   * NSE bhavcopy -- ingestion_file_state shows every recent session's file was first
#     processed the NEXT MORNING (~07:20 IST), never by the 17:30 EOD run. NSE publishes
#     sec_bhavdata_full after 17:30, so that run could not have succeeded.
#   * Dhan EOD bars -- every logged 18:45 reconcile reported current=0 of ~2,880 symbols.
#     Dhan publishes staggered through the evening; this repo's own
#     DATA_READINESS_DHAN_TODAY_AFTER_HOUR_IST default is 23, i.e. the code already knew.
#   * FBIL G-Sec -- published early evening; asking before ~18:00 IST returns nothing and
#     used to mark the whole run "partial" (fixed in download_fbil_gsec.py).
#
# EVENING = best effort, as early as the data plausibly exists:
#   19:15 complete_data     (was 17:30 -- before NSE published)
#   20:30 downloaders queue (new retry slot, second chance the same evening)
#   21:00 fundamentals_screener
#   22:00 portfolio_ruleset  (exits, then entries -- reads the screener's confluence scores)
#   23:05 ohlcv_reconcile   (was 18:45 -- >4h before Dhan had anything)
#   23:25 price_adjustment  (was 18:50 -- ran on whatever was in the DB, often stale)
#   23:40 dhan_intraday_sync
#
# MORNING = the guarantee, and it runs Mon-SATURDAY (1-6), not Mon-Fri.
#   BUG FOUND LIVE 2026-09-06: every recovery job was weekday-only, so a FRIDAY-evening
#   miss had no catch-up until Monday 07:10 IST. That is exactly what happened on
#   2026-09-04: NSE had not published sec_bhavdata_full when the 19:15 run asked, and
#   Friday's bhavcopy then sat missing all weekend -- a whole-weekend hole in the very
#   design that was supposed to be "the guarantee". Saturday morning closes it, because
#   Friday's file is reliably published by then. The evening chain stays 1-5: Saturday is
#   not a trading day, so there is no Saturday session to collect.
#   07:10 complete_data -> 07:30 data_readiness --fix -> 07:40 ohlcv_reconcile
#   -> 07:45 price_adjustment -> 08:00 completeness GATE -> 08:10/08:15 reporting
#
# Ordering is load-bearing: the gate and both reporting jobs sit AFTER the catch-up so
# they judge final data. The gate used to run at 22:50, before the session's bhavcopy was
# even published, and duly failed on its first night for data that was merely late.
# A gate that cries wolf nightly is a gate nobody reads.
#
# No two jobs share a firing minute -- fundamentals_screener was deliberately moved off
# the 20:30 queue slot because both drive Chrome/CDP and concurrent CDP use has caused a
# connect timeout here before.


# Late-night data catch-up: Dhan publishes EOD bars staggered (only a fraction of the
# universe has them at the 18:45 reconcile), and a bad morning bhavcopy fetch must not
# survive the night. Checks bhavcopy/Dhan/benchmark coverage and runs bounded fixes.
# 17:00 UTC = 22:30 IST
00 02 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_data_readiness.lock ./all_data_readiness.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/data_readiness.log" 2>&1

# Daily coverage/staleness report across every KEEP table (docs/DATA_COVERAGE.md).
# Non-fatal visibility layer, not a gate: writes to data_coverage_report (queryable
# trend history) and the log below. Runs after data_readiness so its own freshness
# reflects that pass's fixes.
# 17:10 UTC = 22:40 IST
40 02 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_data_coverage_report.lock ./all_data_coverage_report.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/data_coverage_report.log" 2>&1

# Digest of open identity issues + recent fallback telemetry -- the read/summarize half
# of the write-only advisory_identity_issues / advisory_fallback_events tables (recorded
# but never surfaced, confirmed live 2026-08-14; docs/DATA_COVERAGE.md's "Still open"
# list). Runs right after data_coverage_report so this reflects the same nightly pass.
# 17:15 UTC = 22:45 IST
45 02 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_issue_digest.lock ./all_issue_digest.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/issue_digest.log" 2>&1

# Final verdict on the night's data: is it actually THERE, across the whole universe?
# Added 2026-08-31 after Dhan collection died for 5 days with every job still exiting 0.
# Two things make this different from data_readiness above, and both are deliberate:
#   - it checks BREADTH, not just freshness. The old checks all asked "how recent is
#     the newest row?", which the Dhan connectivity smoke test kept answering "today"
#     for one single ticker while the other ~2,590 were dead.
#   - it imports nothing browser- or broker-related. data_readiness was itself crashing
#     on the same dead-Chrome CDP timeout as the collectors it was meant to be watching,
#     which is exactly why nobody found out for five days.
# Read-only: it never repairs. Exits non-zero on a hard error.

# Daily log rotation before the morning jobs: archive sizable logs as
# logs/cron/archive/<name>.<YYYY-MM-DD>.log.gz (copy-then-truncate so long-running
# processes keep their handles) and prune archives past LOG_ROTATE_KEEP_DAYS.
# 01:20 UTC = 06:50 IST
20 01 * * * {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_log_rotate.lock "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/rotate_logs.sh" >> "$LOG_DIR/rotate_logs.log" 2>&1

# Daily broad raw download + parse safety net before market open on weekdays.
# A second end-of-day complete_data.sh run below repairs anything intraday jobs missed.
# 01:40 UTC = 07:10 IST
40 01 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_complete_data.lock ./complete_data.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/complete_data.log" 2>&1

# --- Morning catch-up: the previous session's data is not final until this runs ---
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-09-01, caught by the completeness gate on its FIRST night):
# NSE publishes the daily bhavcopy around 18:00-19:00 IST, but the EOD complete_data
# run fires at 17:30 IST -- BEFORE it exists. The 18:45 reconcile and 18:50 price
# adjustment then process whatever is in the DB at that moment, which on a slow
# publishing day is still yesterday's data. Confirmed live for 2026-08-31: EOD ran
# clean at 17:42 IST, reconcile and adjustment both ran on stale input, and the
# session's bhavcopy only landed on the 07:10 IST morning run the next day -- leaving
# 2,879 EQ/BE bars with no adjustment factor, silently absent from systrader's PRIMARY
# series, exactly the failure of 2026-08-26..31.
#
# The evening pass is kept (when NSE is prompt it works, and earlier data is better).
# These two re-runs are the guarantee. Both are cheap when there is nothing to do:
# price_adjustment now writes ZERO rows on a no-change run (on_conflict=
# update_if_changed), and ohlcv_reconcile only targets symbols that are actually stale.
# Dhan token refresh -- MUST precede the morning Dhan work. Tokens expire ~20:35 UTC
# (02:05 IST) and the catch-up reconcile below runs at 02:10 UTC, five minutes later.
# Confirmed live 2026-09-04: the evening chain (17:45/18:10 UTC) sits inside the token's
# life and succeeded on ~1412 symbols; the morning pass ran on a dead token and failed
# ~950 of 1500, because an expired token on the daily endpoint returns
# 400 "Missing required fields..." which the client's auth-error predicate does not
# match, so it never refreshed. See all_dhan_auth_ensure.sh for why the predicate was
# not loosened instead.
# 02:05 UTC = 07:35 IST
05 02 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_dhan_auth_ensure.lock ./all_dhan_auth_ensure.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/dhan_auth_ensure.log" 2>&1
# MONDAY ONLY, 01:25 UTC = 06:55 IST -- added 2026-10-08. A token lives ~24h, so Friday's
# expires Saturday 07:35 IST and nothing renews it over the weekend: the 07:10 IST Monday
# complete_data ran its Dhan precheck on a dead token and failed (2026-10-05). This run mints
# Monday's login before it; the 07:35 run above then finds >12h left (--min-fresh-minutes
# 720) and skips, so Monday still mints exactly ONE consent. Tue-Fri need no early run: the
# previous day's 07:35 token is still valid at 07:10, and Saturday's 07:10 run is inside
# Friday's token's life.
25 01 * * 1 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_dhan_auth_ensure.lock ./all_dhan_auth_ensure.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/dhan_auth_ensure.log" 2>&1

# 06:30 UTC = 12:00 IST -- MOVED from 02:10 UTC (07:40 IST) on 2026-09-23. Dhan's daily
# endpoint is unreliable in the 07:40 IST window: measured the same day, the same bulk
# code completed 289/1500 symbols at 07:40, 177/200 at 12:00 and ~1410/1500 at 23:15,
# and symbols that failed at 07:40 returned their bars on a manual retry hours later.
# The backlog that built up behind those failures is why daily coverage sat at ~900 of
# ~2,900 symbols. Midday costs a partial bar for the live session, which the 23:05 IST
# pass overwrites (sync_daily_ohlcv writes update_if_changed for exactly this reason).
30 06 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_ohlcv_reconcile.lock ./all_ohlcv_reconcile.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/ohlcv_reconcile.log" 2>&1

# 02:15 UTC = 07:45 IST -- after the morning complete_data has landed the bhavcopy (the
# reconcile that used to sit at 02:10 moved to 06:30 UTC; price adjustment does not
# depend on it, only on the bhavcopy)
15 02 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_price_adjustment.lock ./all_price_adjustment.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/price_adjustment.log" 2>&1

# Completeness gate -- MOVED here from 22:50 IST on 2026-09-01. It has to run after the
# catch-up above, not before: at 22:50 the previous session's bhavcopy legitimately may
# not have been published yet, so the gate failed on its first night for data that was
# merely late rather than lost. A gate that fails most nights for a benign reason
# teaches the operator to ignore it, which is the one thing it must never do.
# 02:30 UTC = 08:00 IST
30 02 * * 1-6 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_data_completeness.lock ./all_data_completeness.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/data_completeness.log" 2>&1

# Queue single-client downloader work and drain it without parallel NSE/Dhan/Screener sessions.
# The direct complete_data.sh path remains the broad catch-up/backfill safety net.
# all_external_workers.sh is NOT optional: all_downloaders_queue.sh routes every
# data.nseindia.* module plus Dhan scrip_master/ohlcv into the nse/dhan queues instead of
# running them inline -- this is the only thing that drains those queues (see DATA_INVENTORY.md).
# 03:00,07:00,11:00 UTC = 08:30,12:30,16:30 IST
00 03,07,11,15 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_download_queue.lock ./all_downloaders_queue.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/all_downloaders_queue.log" 2>&1
# 03:05,07:05,11:05 UTC = 08:35,12:35,16:35 IST
05 03,07,11,15 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_external_workers.lock ./all_external_workers.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/external_workers.log" 2>&1

# End-of-day broad catch-up. This intentionally runs the full download+parse path so any
# downloader/parser work missed earlier in the day is repaired.
# 12:00 UTC = 17:30 IST
45 13 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_complete_data.lock ./complete_data.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/complete_data_eod.log" 2>&1

# Daily OHLCV coverage reconciliation. Backfills any universe symbol whose latest daily bar
# predates the last completed trading day (e.g. after the scheduler was down during market
# hours), so systrader never reads silently stale bars.
# 13:15 UTC = 18:45 IST
45 17 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_ohlcv_reconcile.lock ./all_ohlcv_reconcile.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/ohlcv_reconcile.log" 2>&1

# Split/bonus-adjusted price table (price-step derived) -- systrader's PRIMARY equity series
# (advisory_adjusted_ohlcv_daily), promoted out of advisory/ 2026-07-28. Scheduled right after
# the OHLCV reconcile now that the downstream advisory/research chain that used to sit between
# them is gone -- no need to wait until 21:38 anymore.
# 13:20 UTC = 18:50 IST
30 14 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_price_adjustment.lock ./all_price_adjustment.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/price_adjustment.log" 2>&1

# Daily incremental Dhan 1-min intraday OHLCV sync for the full active NSE equity
# universe (data/dhanlive/intraday_daily_sync.py) -- HF_DATA_PLATFORM_PLAN.md
# (systrader repo), 2026-08-22: companion to the one-time 5-year historical
# backfill (scripts/backfill_intraday_5yr.py, run manually, not scheduled).
# Independent of the fundamentals screener below (different tables, no
# dependency either way) -- scheduled right after price_adjustment purely so
# the day's EOD data is settled first.
# 13:25 UTC = 18:55 IST
10 18 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_dhan_intraday_sync.lock ./all_dhan_intraday_sync.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/dhan_intraday_sync.log" 2>&1

# Fundamentals screener pipeline: L1/L2 refresh, event collectors, OCR + structured
# extraction, sector capital-cycle, L3 alerts (rule + LLM triage), descriptive
# technicals, and the watchlist/narrative/email pipeline (fundamentals/run_pipeline.py,
# one step failing does not abort the run). Scheduled after price_adjustment
# (18:50 IST) so the descriptive-technicals step reads a same-day adjusted price series.
# 13:45 UTC = 19:15 IST
30 15 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_fundamentals_screener.lock ./all_fundamentals_screener.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/fundamentals_screener.log" 2>&1

# Portfolio ruleset + LLM adjudication (docs/PORTFOLIO_RULESET_PRD.md): the mechanical
# entry rule, the entry adjudicator (which may only REJECT), the mechanical exit
# evaluator, and the exit adjudicator (which may only DEFER, and never a stop).
# Scheduled an hour after fundamentals_screener (21:00 IST) because it reads that run's
# fundamentals_confluence_score output, plus systrader's stage API for the price read.
# RECORD-ONLY: --live is deliberately NOT passed -- rollout phase 1 commits no money.
# 16:30 UTC = 22:00 IST
30 16 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_portfolio_ruleset.lock ./all_portfolio_ruleset.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/portfolio_ruleset.log" 2>&1

# Economic Times RSS news (fundamentals/collectors/et_news.py), hourly at :07 -- not gated on
# .pause_fundamentals (feeds keep only 50 items; a skipped hour is lost news).
7 * * * * {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_fundamentals_news.lock ./all_fundamentals_news.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/fundamentals_news.log" 2>&1

# Event-driven re-evaluation (all_fundamentals_reeval.sh; FUNDAMENTAL_REEVALUATION_PRD 4.2):
# today's new BSE filings -> extraction -> rule triggers -> news tagging -> re-score, at :17
# and :47 (off the OCR, news and API minutes). Gated on .pause_fundamentals, and stands aside
# while the nightly screener runs.
17,47 * * * * {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_fundamentals_reeval.lock ./all_fundamentals_reeval.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/fundamentals_reeval.log" 2>&1

# OCR of filed documents (fundamentals/collectors/ocr_pipeline.py), its own continuous job
# since 2026-09-25 -- see all_fundamentals_ocr.sh. Every 30 minutes, under a lock, so a
# long catch-up run is never doubled; not gated on .pause_fundamentals.
*/30 * * * * {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_fundamentals_ocr.lock ./all_fundamentals_ocr.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/fundamentals_ocr.log" 2>&1

# Fundamentals screener API (fundamentals/api/app.py), serving the screener/ Nuxt
# frontend. Long-running service, same respawn-under-lock pattern the old
# all_frontend.sh used (see stockey-service-management memory): cron retries every 5
# minutes, with_lock.sh no-ops while a real instance holds the lock, and the script's
# own /api/health check no-ops again if something is already serving. No weekday
# restriction -- this is a local dashboard, not a market-hours job.
# Every 5 minutes, wall-clock -- not IST-anchored, no conversion needed.
*/5 * * * * {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_fundamentals_api.lock ./all_fundamentals_api.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/fundamentals_api.log" 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manual / catch-up / long-running scripts. Keep these commented unless you
# intentionally want extra end-of-day repair jobs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Optional split refreshes if you want explicit control instead of complete_data.sh.
# 01:35 UTC = 07:05 IST
# 35 01 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_downloaders.lock ./all_downloaders.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/all_downloaders.log" 2>&1
# 02:10 UTC = 07:40 IST
# 10 02 * * 1-5 {{STOCKEY_USER}} cd "$STOCKEY_DIR" && mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && "$STOCKEY_DIR/scripts/with_lock.sh" /tmp/stockey_parsers.lock ./all_parsers.sh >> "$LOG_DIR/all_parsers.log" 2>&1
